From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:47:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): read stored open items in the panel, badge and
 chips

The Open items panel, its header badge and the label chips read item state
from the chat text in the browser, so they depend on how much history is
loaded, and an item an agent closed with sys_open_items_update stays open
in the panel until the chat strikes it. Servers with the open items store
keep the real state.

Where /v1/info reports open_items, the web reads every stored item of the
session (GET /v1/sessions/{id}/open-items, all statuses) and keeps the list
current with session.open_items.changed and a re-read when the session
stream reopens. One index merges the two: a stored label takes its state
from the store everywhere (chips, popovers, panel, badge), and a label only
the chat has keeps the chat's state, listed as "chat only". The panel lists
stored items by status (latest reply first, open, answered, closed folded),
expands a row to its detail, links, answers and resolution, and lets a
person with edit access close (one tap, or with a resolution), reopen and
retopic items through PATCH. Dismissing a stored item becomes a user close:
the omnigent.items_dismissed label is no longer written for stored items,
and is still read for chat-only ones. A stored item the chat struck while
the store keeps it open is flagged with a one-tap Close.

Without the capability, or when the list cannot be read, everything renders
from the chat as before.

Not proposed upstream yet: the store and the panel it extends are not
upstream either.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
